---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import '../styles/doc.css';
import { ATH_USD_TEXT } from '../lib/ath.js';
import HeroEmblem from '../components/HeroEmblem.astro';
---
<Base title="Bitcoin History: The Full Timeline, 2008 to Now - OpenBitcoin" description="A timeline of bitcoin's history: the 2008 whitepaper, the genesis block, pizza day, Mt. Gox, the halvings, the ETFs, and each all-time high, with prices.">
<main class="wrap doc-wrap">
  <div class="doc-head">
    <div class="doc-kicker">History</div>
    <h1>The bitcoin timeline</h1>
    <HeroEmblem name="hourglass" />
    <p class="doc-lede">From a nine-page paper on a mailing list to a national currency and a Wall Street fund, in seventeen years. Twenty-two moments that mattered, in order, each with the approximate price of one bitcoin on that day.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="doc-grid">
  <div>
    <div class="hi-tl" id="hi-tl">

      <div class="hi-ev" id="y2008">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2008</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">October 31, 2008</span><span class="hi-px hi-px-na">no market price</span></div>
          <h2>The whitepaper</h2>
          <p>Someone using the name Satoshi Nakamoto posts a nine-page paper, <em>Bitcoin: A Peer-to-Peer Electronic Cash System</em>, to a cryptography mailing list. It describes electronic cash that needs no bank in the middle. The <a href="/learn/whitepaper">paper</a> still reads in one sitting; the author's identity is <a href="/learn/who-is-satoshi">still unknown</a>.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2009</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">January 3, 2009</span><span class="hi-px hi-px-na">no market price</span></div>
          <h2>The genesis block</h2>
          <p>Satoshi mines block zero. Embedded in it, permanently, is that day's front page of The Times of London: <em>Chancellor on brink of second bailout for banks</em>. Part timestamp, part statement of purpose. The 50 coins in the genesis block can never be spent.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">January 12, 2009</span><span class="hi-px hi-px-na">no market price</span></div>
          <h2>The first transaction</h2>
          <p>In block 170, Satoshi sends 10 BTC to the cryptographer Hal Finney, the first transfer of bitcoin from one person to another. Finney had announced himself the day before with a two-word post: "Running bitcoin." For months, the network is a handful of computers kept alive by people who find the idea interesting.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">February 11, 2009</span><span class="hi-px hi-px-na">no market price</span></div>
          <h2>Satoshi explains why</h2>
          <p>Announcing the software on the P2P Foundation forum, Satoshi states the case in two sentences that have not aged:</p>
          <blockquote class="hi-quote">The root problem with conventional currency is all the trust that's required to make it work. The central bank must be trusted not to debase the currency, but the history of fiat currencies is full of breaches of that trust.
            <span class="hi-qattr">Satoshi Nakamoto, P2P Foundation forum</span>
          </blockquote>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">October 5, 2009</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $0.0008</span></div>
          <h2>The first exchange rate</h2>
          <p>A service called New Liberty Standard publishes the first known price: $1 buys 1,309.03 BTC, calculated from the electricity it cost to mine. Bitcoin now has a market value, and it is less than a tenth of a cent. In this era coins are also simply given away; <a href="/history/faucets">the faucet story</a> covers that.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev" id="y2010">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2010</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">May 22, 2010</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $0.004</span></div>
          <h2>Pizza day</h2>
          <p>A Florida programmer pays 10,000 BTC, then quoted around $41, for two delivered pizzas: the first widely documented purchase of physical goods with bitcoin. The date is now an annual holiday and a standing lesson in what small, regular amounts can become; the <a href="/dca">averaging calculator</a> runs that arithmetic on any schedule you like.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">July 18, 2010</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $0.05</span></div>
          <h2>Mt. Gox opens</h2>
          <p>A domain built for trading Magic: The Gathering cards relaunches as a bitcoin exchange. Twenty coins trade on day one, at about five cents each. Within a few years Mt. Gox handles most of the world's bitcoin trading, which makes what happens in 2014 matter to almost everyone.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev hi-ev-key" id="y2012">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2012</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">November 28, 2012</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $12</span></div>
          <h2>The first halving</h2>
          <p>At block 210,000 the reward for mining a block drops from 50 BTC to 25, exactly as the code always said it would. The supply schedule holds without anyone's permission, and it has held at every <a href="/halving">halving</a> since.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev" id="y2013">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2013</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">October 2, 2013</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $114</span></div>
          <h2>Silk Road seized</h2>
          <p>The FBI arrests the operator of the Silk Road marketplace in a San Francisco library and shuts the site down. The price closes near $114, down sharply on the day. The episode fixes bitcoin's outlaw reputation in the public mind, and the market recovers within weeks anyway.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">November 28, 2013</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $1,000</span></div>
          <h2>The 2013 run</h2>
          <p>Bitcoin crosses $1,000 for the first time. It is the year's second bubble: April touched $266 before a fast collapse, and the autumn run tops out near $1,163. Bitcoin has now been declared dead dozens of times; the <a href="/obituaries">obituary count</a> keeps the receipts.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev" id="y2014">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2014</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">February 28, 2014</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $550</span></div>
          <h2>Mt. Gox collapses</h2>
          <p>The exchange that handled most of the world's bitcoin halts withdrawals in early February, then files for bankruptcy in Tokyo, admitting that about 850,000 BTC are gone: roughly 750,000 belonging to customers and 100,000 of its own. It remains the defining lesson in why an exchange balance is not the same thing as bitcoin; <a href="/learn/frozen-deposits">frozen deposits</a> traces what customers went through, and the <a href="/hacks">hacks record</a> puts the theft beside every other major one.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev hi-ev-key" id="y2016">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2016</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">July 9, 2016</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $650</span></div>
          <h2>The second halving</h2>
          <p>Block 420,000 cuts the reward from 25 BTC to 12.5. The network processes it without incident, at around $650, and the <a href="/halving">schedule</a> ticks on toward the next one.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev" id="y2017">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2017</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">August 24, 2017</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $4,300</span></div>
          <h2>Segwit activates</h2>
          <p>After years of public argument over how bitcoin should scale, the Segregated Witness upgrade activates at block 481,824. It increases capacity, fixes transaction malleability, and clears the path for the Lightning network. The block size war ends with the conservative side holding the name.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">December 17, 2017</span><span class="hi-px">$19,783</span></div>
          <h2>The 2017 peak</h2>
          <p>The retail mania year ends with bitcoin at $19,783 on CoinDesk's index, up from under $1,000 in January. Futures launch on US exchanges the same month. Nearly everyone who bought that December waits three years to break even.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev" id="y2018">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2018</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">December 15, 2018</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $3,200</span></div>
          <h2>The winter</h2>
          <p>A year of steady decline bottoms near $3,200, roughly 84 percent below the peak. The <a href="/obituaries">obituaries</a> pile up again. The network itself never misses a block.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev" id="y2020">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2020</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">March 12, 2020</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $4,800</span></div>
          <h2>The covid crash, then the treasuries</h2>
          <p>As markets everywhere seize up, bitcoin falls from near $8,000 to around $4,700 in hours, lower still on some venues. Five months later the first US-listed company moves $250 million of its treasury into 21,454 BTC, and the corporate treasury era begins from the wreckage of the panic.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev hi-ev-key">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">May 11, 2020</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $8,600</span></div>
          <h2>The third halving</h2>
          <p>Block 630,000, two months after the crash: the reward drops from 12.5 BTC to 6.25. Three halvings in, the event has become routine, which is the point. The <a href="/halving">halving page</a> tracks the countdown to each one.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev" id="y2021">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2021</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">September 7, 2021</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $47,000</span></div>
          <h2>El Salvador, legal tender</h2>
          <p>El Salvador becomes the first country to make bitcoin legal tender. The market marks the occasion with a lurch: from around $52,000 toward $43,000 and partway back inside the day. A currency born on a mailing list is now written into a nation's law.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev" id="y2022">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2022</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">November 11, 2022</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $17,000</span></div>
          <h2>FTX falls</h2>
          <p>The FTX exchange files for bankruptcy, the last and largest of a year of custodial failures that had already taken Terra and the lenders Celsius and Voyager. The price dips near $16,400. The losses land almost entirely on people who left coins with companies; <a href="/learn/frozen-deposits">frozen deposits</a> is the pattern, retold at scale.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev" id="y2024">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2024</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">January 11, 2024</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $46,000</span></div>
          <h2>The US spot ETFs</h2>
          <p>Approved on January 10 after a decade of rejections, eleven spot bitcoin <a href="/learn/etf">ETFs</a> begin trading in the United States and do $4.6 billion in volume on day one. Retirement accounts and brokerages can now hold bitcoin exposure without touching a wallet, for better and for worse.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev hi-ev-key">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">April 20, 2024</span><span class="hi-px">&asymp; $64,000</span></div>
          <h2>The fourth halving</h2>
          <p>Block 840,000 cuts the reward from 6.25 BTC to 3.125. For the first time, a <a href="/halving">halving</a> arrives with the price near an all-time high rather than deep in a trough.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="hi-ev hi-ev-key" id="y2025">
        <span class="hi-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span class="hi-yr">2025</span>
        <article class="hi-card">
          <div class="hi-meta"><span class="hi-date">October 6, 2025</span><span class="hi-px">{ATH_USD_TEXT}</span></div>
          <h2>The all-time high</h2>
          <p>Bitcoin records its highest price to date, {ATH_USD_TEXT}. Sixteen years earlier, the first published rate valued the entire day's mining at fractions of a cent. Where the price stands against the peak right now is on the <a href="/ath">all-time high page</a>.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="hi-about doc-prose">
      <p>The shape of the story repeats: a run, a collapse, a round of <a href="/obituaries">obituaries</a>, and a network that keeps producing blocks through all of it. The people are stranger than the price chart; the author of the whitepaper <a href="/learn/who-is-satoshi">has never been identified</a>, and the early years when coins were handed out free are a story of their own, told in <a href="/history/faucets">the faucet era</a>. For the one constant that runs under every entry above, the supply schedule, see the <a href="/halving">halving page</a>; for where the story stands this minute, the <a href="/price">live price</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <aside class="doc-rail">
    <div class="doc-tile">
      <div class="doc-tlab">Right now</div>
      <div class="hi-stat"><b id="hi-now-px">&#8230;</b><i>1 BTC</i></div>
      <div class="hi-stat"><b id="hi-now-ht">&#8230;</b><i>block height</i></div>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-tile">
      <div class="doc-tlab">Jump to</div>
      <nav>
        <a href="#y2008">2008: the paper</a>
        <a href="#y2010">2010: first prices</a>
        <a href="#y2013">2013: the first run</a>
        <a href="#y2017">2017: the mania</a>
        <a href="#y2020">2020: the crash</a>
        <a href="#y2024">2024: the ETFs</a>
        <a href="#y2025">2025: the high</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
    <div class="doc-tile">
      <div class="doc-tlab">Related</div>
      <nav>
        <a href="/history/people">The people of early bitcoin</a>
        <a href="/obituaries">Bitcoin obituaries</a>
        <a href="/hacks">The largest bitcoin hacks</a>
        <a href="/halving">The halving schedule</a>
        <a href="/learn/who-is-satoshi">Who is Satoshi?</a>
        <a href="/history/faucets">The faucet era</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </aside>
  </div>
</main>
<style is:global>
  .hi-tl{position:relative;margin-top:4px;padding-left:88px}
  .hi-tl::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:64px;top:10px;bottom:10px;width:2px;border-radius:1px;
    background:linear-gradient(180deg,rgba(247,147,26,.55),var(--line-2) 10%,var(--line-2) 90%,rgba(247,147,26,.55))}
  .hi-ev{position:relative;margin-top:16px;scroll-margin-top:18px}
  .hi-ev:first-child{margin-top:0}
  .hi-dot{position:absolute;left:-29px;top:20px;width:12px;height:12px;border-radius:50%;
    background:var(--bg);border:2px solid var(--acc);box-shadow:0 0 0 3px var(--bg)}
  .hi-ev-key .hi-dot{background:var(--acc)}
  .hi-yr{position:absolute;left:-88px;top:20px;width:50px;text-align:right;
    font:700 12px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--ink-3);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  .hi-ev-key .hi-yr{color:var(--acc)}
  .hi-card{background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:16px 20px 17px}
  .hi-meta{display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:space-between;gap:8px 12px;flex-wrap:wrap}
  .hi-date{font:700 9.5px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3)}
  .hi-px{font:700 11px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.04em;color:var(--acc);background:var(--field);
    border:1px dotted var(--line-2);border-radius:6px;padding:3px 8px;white-space:nowrap;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  .hi-px-na{color:var(--ink-3)}
  .hi-card h2{font:700 16px/1.3 var(--sans);color:var(--ink);margin:8px 0 0}
  .hi-card p{font:500 13.5px/1.65 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-2);margin:8px 0 0}
  .hi-card em{font-style:italic;color:var(--ink)}
  .hi-card a{color:var(--acc);text-decoration:none;border-bottom:1px dashed rgba(247,147,26,.35);padding-bottom:1px}
  .hi-card a:hover{border-bottom-style:solid}
  .hi-quote{margin:10px 0 0;padding:11px 15px;background:var(--panel-2);border-left:2px solid var(--acc);
    border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;font:500 13.5px/1.65 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-2)}
  .hi-qattr{display:block;margin-top:7px;font:700 9px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3)}
  .hi-about{margin-top:16px}
  .hi-about p{font:500 13.5px/1.65 var(--sans);color:var(--ink-3)}
  .hi-stat{padding:7px 0;border-bottom:1px dotted var(--line-2)}
  .hi-stat:last-child{border-bottom:0}
  .hi-stat b{display:block;font:700 16px var(--mono);color:var(--ink);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
  .hi-stat i{display:block;font:600 9px var(--mono);letter-spacing:.11em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--ink-3);font-style:normal;margin-top:2px}
  
  .hi-anim .hi-ev{opacity:0;transform:translateY(14px);transition:opacity .55s ease,transform .55s ease}
  .hi-anim .hi-in{opacity:1;transform:none}
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce){
    .hi-anim .hi-ev{opacity:1;transform:none;transition:none}
  }
  @media(max-width:700px){
    .hi-tl{padding-left:26px}
    .hi-tl::before{left:6px}
    .hi-dot{left:-24px;top:19px;width:10px;height:10px}
    .hi-yr{position:static;display:inline-block;width:auto;text-align:left;margin:0 0 6px}
    .hi-card{padding:14px 15px 16px}
  }
</style>
<script is:inline>
(function(){
  var P={price:null,height:null};
  function fmt(n){return n.toLocaleString("en-US",{maximumFractionDigits:0});}
  var px=document.getElementById("hi-now-px"),ht=document.getElementById("hi-now-ht");
  function paint(){
    if(px&&P.price)px.textContent="$"+fmt(P.price);
    if(ht&&P.height)ht.textContent=fmt(P.height);
  }
  /* live price and height arrive via the chrome hook; window.OB_LIVE is only
     set once a real summary lands, so the ellipses hold until then */
  window.obPaintFiat=function(S){if(!window.OB_LIVE)return;if(S.price)P.price=S.price;if(S.height)P.height=S.height;paint();};
  /* scroll reveal: only when the browser supports it and motion is allowed */
  var tl=document.getElementById("hi-tl");
  var reduce=window.matchMedia&&window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches;
  if(tl&&"IntersectionObserver" in window&&!reduce){
    tl.classList.add("hi-anim");
    var evs=tl.querySelectorAll(".hi-ev");
    var io=new IntersectionObserver(function(entries){
      for(var i=0;i<entries.length;i++){
        if(entries[i].isIntersecting){entries[i].target.classList.add("hi-in");io.unobserve(entries[i].target);}
      }
    },{rootMargin:"0px 0px -10% 0px",threshold:0.05});
    for(var j=0;j<evs.length;j++)io.observe(evs[j]);
  }
})();
</script>
</Base>
